# TUI-DESIGN-5 §9.3 W5 / §13 — the round-5 live leg. A zero-argument `jevcode` against live Jev through TypeSafe
# native (JEV_PROVIDER auto → typesafe from TYPESAFE_API_KEY in the repository's ./.env), the generator key unset
# in the environment (`env -u ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`), a temp JEVCODE_HOME, the workspace a fresh copy of
# examples/demo-py (git init, .venv with pytest). Reviews are answered by the driver (PTY_AUTO_REVIEW=y). Every
# pause is a draining `sleep` (research 20 §5). Every anchor is glyph-agnostic (`[·-]`, §13.4).
#
# Round 5's two new READS are driven here beside round 4's hero path: `/who` (§2.3, the coordination surface) and
# `/context` (§3.2, the context meter). Both are `availableDuringTask: 'any'`, both answer honestly when their
# store is not open, and BOTH are asserted for key bytes by `summarize.py` afterwards (gate G-R5-9).
expect \x1b\[\?25l
mark first-frame
expect step 0/
expect \x1b\[\?2004h
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
mark composer-ready
# the splash settles by itself into the version caption
expect ◆(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*\d+\.\d+\.\d+
mark splash-settled
sleep 0.3
# a greeting: one Jev intake request, a [you] bubble, a [jevcode] reply, no run
send hi
sleep 0.2
send \r
mark hi-sent
expect \[you\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*hi
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* 
mark hi-reply
sleep 0.5
# §2.3: `/who` before any run. The ledger is not open yet, so the honest answer is the head plus its note —
# never a false zero and never a spinner (§1.4 promise 1).
send /who
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect who
mark who-idle
sleep 0.3
# §3.2 / §7 row 35: `/context` with no live run is S54's own sentence, not an empty block
send /context
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect context
mark context-idle
sleep 0.3
# a real task under the llm-jev default: the run frame, the review card if one appears (PTY_AUTO_REVIEW)
send Fix the failing tests in tests/test_core.py without changing the tests.
sleep 0.3
send \r
mark task-sent
expect \[run\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*started [·-] 
mark run-started
expect \[step 1\]
mark step-1
expect finished [·-] (complete|max_steps|spend_cap|wall_time|human_pause|replan_stop|impossible|error)
mark run-ended
sleep 0.5
# §3.2 with a run behind it: the three reads join into ONE block (the budget row is `formatBudget`'s own text)
send /context
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect context
mark context-after-run
sleep 0.3
# round 4's kv block grammar, unchanged by round 5. After a task the intake row counts BOTH submissions (the greeting
# and the task text are each one Jev intake request), so the row reads `intake     2 messages · …`, not `1 message`;
# the integration pass copied round 4's PRE-run expectation here and both drives timed out on it (2026-09-22).
send /jev
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect intake {2,}\d+ messages?
mark jev-after-run
sleep 0.3
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
